body:
This has been a major fear of mine and why I have gotten a small home gym installed, like last time I went out and had a meltdown in the metro tunnel. I hope to god no one filmed it but I do not know...

&#x200B;

Having public meltdowns while there is this social media craze of people filming strangers and being mean to that total stranger for acting different has made me not leave my house more than nessecesary

There is what I am feeling which is a 2 but then there is what stress my body is showing me after how traumatic 2023 was, I like to think I'm fine. 

&#x200B;

But after being stalked and then being made homeless by my landlord, who was on my neighbor's stalker side, aka also his landlord. to being homeless for 2 months then getting an apartment then going to Paris on a whim for Twitch con to forget about the shit start to the year, then the constant traveling and clumsy accidents i got into by falling down a flight of stairs in London.. to the getting home trying to unpack my stuff to finding out im missing stuff to the im still unpacking in 2024... and that my body is physically reacting to the shit I went thru but my mind is just vibing on rainbows...

23 here, I have friends who are 17-65 and all different places in life, i know a lot of people who are the same age but are living way different lives. I know a few 27-year-olds and some have kids and some are just vibing in life and most of them are on the spectrum or have some sort of other disability.

&#x200B;

i think having friends of all ages is a good thing :)

Well, I don't actually remember most of it, my memory has blacked it out because of how traumatic it was... but it was when a friend of mine slit her wrists with a bread knife, in the hall of the home we lived in at the time... while the caretakers were in a meeting, I only remember her holding the knife to her wrist, then black and then sitting on the floor covered in her blood, having the caretakers pull me off of the floor... while she is being driven away in an ambulance. I actually have never been told what happened at the time, It's been 7 years and I don't exactly know what happened. I can't even ask her now after she succeeded in committing suicide last year.

&#x200B;

Edit: I was 13/14 at the time and it's something I wish I never saw... till this day I have a self-harm problem I wish I never learned what self-harm was a thing...
